          <p>
            If those panel numbers look large, that is the honest picture. A big battery bridges a night; only a matching array bridges a week. For outages measured in weeks, or for central air and electric heat, a standby system is still the tool, and our <a href="/generac-generator-cost/">standby generator cost guide</a> shows what that involves. Many households land on a hybrid: a solar generator for silent nights and daily essentials, and a small inverter generator from our <a href="/best-small-generator-for-home/">small home generator picks</a> to refill the battery during a long run of cloud.
          </p>
